config.h started as a copy of config.def.h. Edit config.h; keep
config.def.h as upstream so new releases can be compared against it.

One change from upstream in config.def.h too: MODKEY is Mod4Mask (Super)
instead of Mod1Mask (Alt), to match the Moonlander dwm layer.

Patches (originals from dwm.suckless.org/patches, kept in patches/,
applied in this order; dwm.c already has them, so don't apply again):
  alwayscenter       dwm-alwayscenter-20200625-f04cac6.diff
  attachbelow        dwm-attachbelow-6.2.diff (updategeom hunk by hand)
  scratchpad         dwm-scratchpad-20240321-061e9fe.diff
  combo              dwm-combo-6.1.diff
  noborder           dwm-noborderselflickerfix-2022042627-d93ff48803f0.diff
                     (solitary() prototype by hand)
  pertag             dwm-pertag_with_sel-20231003-9f88553.diff
                     (by hand: the bar is left out, so Mod+b is the same
                     on every tag; comboview goes through view() so a
                     combo uses the settings of its first tag)
  movestack          dwm-movestack-20211115-a786211.diff (movestack.c only)
  doubledeck         dwm-deck-double-6.2.diff
  restart            local, not from suckless.org (the idea of restartsig
                     and preserveonrestart, written for this dwm):
                     Mod+Shift+r or `dwm restart` in a terminal execs dwm
                     again in place. Before that, every window gets its
                     tags, monitor, order and floating geometry as an X
                     property, and the root window each monitor's tags in
                     view and pertag settings (layouts, mfact, nmaster,
                     focused window); the new dwm reads them back. `dwm
                     restart` sends a _DWM_RESTART ClientMessage to the
                     root window. patches/dwm-restart-local.diff.
  resizecorners      local, the idea of the suckless resizecorners patch:
                     Mod+right-drag resizes from the corner nearest the
                     pointer and the opposite corner stays put (size
                     hints applied before the edge moves, so terminals
                     don't drift). Corner cursors for each direction.
                     patches/dwm-resizecorners-local.diff.
  sticky             local, the idea of the suckless sticky patch:
                     Mod+s pins the focused window to every tag of its
                     monitor and floats it. Mod+j/k, tag changes and
                     closing windows never focus it; click it to. Kept
                     over dwm restart. patches/dwm-sticky-local.diff.
  snapwindows        local: moving (Mod+left-drag) and resizing
                     (Mod+right-drag) snap window edges to the edges of
                     other visible windows when they come within winsnap
                     pixels (config.h, 16), as upstream snaps to the
                     screen edges within snap (32). Each edge snaps to
                     both sides of a window it is level with: top to
                     bottom, left to left, and so on. Resizing also snaps
                     the dragged edges to the screen edges, and a snapped
                     edge ignores size increments so it lines up exactly.
                     patches/dwm-snapwindows-local.diff.
  startrules         local: startrules[] in config.h, rules that place
                     only the first matching window in the first minute
                     after login (for apps x/xinitrc starts).
Their config.def.h hunks are not applied (config.def.h stays upstream);
the settings are in config.h.
